NNAAMMEE
       ppmtogif - replaced by pamtogif


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppppmmttooggiiff was replaced in Netpbm 10.37 (December 2006) by ppaammttooggiiff(1).

       ppaammttooggiiff is mostly backward compatible with ppppmmttooggiiff.

       One  way  ppaammttooggiiff  is not backward compatible with ppppmmttooggiiff is that to
       specify a transparency (alpha)  mask  with  ppppmmttooggiiff,  you  supply  the
       transparency  as a separate pseudo-PGM image and use the --aallpphhaa option,
       whereas with ppaammttooggiiff, you supply an input image that has the transpar‐
       ency integrated into it, and there is no --aallpphhaa option.

       ppppmmttooggiiff still exists as a separate program for backward compatibility,
       but it runs ppaammttooggiiff to do the essential work.  The compatibility  ppppmm‐‐
       ttooggiiff interprets an --aallpphhaa option by reading the transparency image and
       combining it with the input image, then feeding ppaammttooggiiff  the  combined
       image  it  expects.   Other  than that, the compatibility ppppmmttooggiiff just
       passes input and options directly to ppaammttooggiiff.

       You should not make any new use of ppppmmttooggiiff and if you modify an exist‐
       ing  use, you should upgrade to ppaammttooggiiff.  But note that if you write a
       program that might have to be used with old  Netpbm,  ppppmmttooggiiff  is  the
       only way to do that.

       Unless you use the --aallpphhaa option, you can simply change the name of the
       program.  If you use --aallpphhaa, here is how to upgrade:

         $ ppmtogif -alpha=myalpha.pgm myinput.ppm >myoutput.gif


       becomes

         $ pamstack -tupletype=RGB_ALPHA myinput.ppm myalpha.pgm |  \
             pamtogif >myoutput.gif




OOrriiggiinnaall PPppmmttooggiiff
       If you are using Netpbm before 10.37, ppaammttooggiiff doesn't  exist,  so  you
       use  ppppmmttooggiiff.   You can use the ppaammttooggiiff manual for ppppmmttooggiiff, with the
       following exceptions.

       The current documentation of ppaammttooggiiff documents all  versions  of  that
       program.  Use the information for Version 10.37 only.

       ppppmmttooggiiff before Netpbm 10.31 does not accept PAM input at all.

       ppppmmttooggiiff does not accept PAM input with transparency information in it.
       Instead, ppppmmttooggiiff has an --aallpphhaa option.

       The syntax of the option is --aallpphhaa==_p_g_m_f_i_l_e.  ppppmmttooggiiff treats  the  con‐
       tents of the named PGM file the same as ppaammttooggiiff treats the alpha plane
       of a PAM.  The PGM image must have the same  dimensions  as  the  input
       file.   But unlike the PAM case, the alpha image need not have the same
       maxval as the input.  ppppmmttooggiiff interprets the alpha file using the  al‐
       pha file's maxval.

       You cannot specify both --ttrraannssppaarreenntt and --aallpphhaa.

